```

Notes:
- `telegram-web-app.js` sets the `--tg-theme-*`, `--tg-viewport-stable-height`, and `--tg-safe-area-inset-*` CSS variables on `document.documentElement` itself and updates them live on `themeChanged`, so no manual listener is needed for colors — the fallback values just make the screen render sensibly outside Telegram.
- `Telegram.WebApp.ready()`/`expand()` belong once at your app root, not in this screen, so they aren't called here.
- Inside real Telegram, `webApp` is truthy and both plain-DOM back/pay buttons stay unmounted — only the host BackButton/MainButton drive navigation and payment, per the platform rule against duplicate controls.
